.TH "PERCH-MAIL" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-mail \- list, search, fetch, send, and inspect mail over IMAP and SMTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch mail [OPTIONS] COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The mail command group is a scriptable IMAP and SMTP client. list, search, and fetch talk IMAP; send talks SMTP; caps prints the SMTP EHLO extensions of a submission server.
.PP
Credentials and TLS flags are shared. IMAP flags are local to list/search/fetch; SMTP flags are local to send/caps.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
If \-\-server or \-\-smtp\-server is omitted, the matching listener is taken from \-\-config.
.IP \(bu 2
Use \-\-plaintext or \-\-smtp\-plaintext only for trusted loopback listeners.
.IP \(bu 2
Password sources: \-\-password\-file, \-\-password\-stdin, PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD, or an interactive prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-username, \-u <value>
account username (env PERCH_IMAP_USER)
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
account password (prefer PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD or \-\-password\-file)
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file <value>
read the account password from a file
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
read the account password from stdin
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <value>
connection timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
list mailboxes (aliases: ls)
.TP
.B search
search message metadata (aliases: find)
.TP
.B fetch
fetch raw messages (aliases: get)
.TP
.B send
compose and send a message
.TP
.B caps
show the SMTP extensions advertised by a submission server (aliases: capabilities)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch mail list \-\-server imaps://mail.example.com \-\-username you@example.com

perch mail search \-q 'unseen from:alice' \-\-json

perch mail fetch \-q 'from:alice' \-\-format mbox > alice.mbox

perch mail send \-\-from you@example.com \-\-to alice@example.com \\
  \-\-subject Hello \-\-body 'Hi Alice'
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_USER
default account username
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD
account password
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\-caps\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\-fetch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\-list\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\-search\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\-send\fR(1)
